From: 4Sakens <4Sakens@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:36:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] host: preludes from a shared pool while their submission runs
 (VICTORY_PRELUDE_POOL)

Each host list kept its own prelude (an allocator and a list for the
transitions before it) from its first submission that needed one until
the list went: 1,140 alive in foxhound's 25-minute run, each pair about
2.9 MB of the PC's memory in the driver. A prelude is used only while
its list's submission runs, so a list now takes one from a pool then
and gives it back at its reset (or when its recycled list is not kept);
the lists in the air hold theirs, about 190. The pool keeps 256 at most.
VICTORY_PRELUDE_POOL=0: each list keeps its own, as before.

From readmet3xt-lab/foxhound 0.2.0-pre.4; VIctory-RDNA takes a prelude
in two places, both from the pool here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6tkVHCftUUQbGm5NirGaG
---
